<VI _name="lvai_run_for_ms.vi" description="Start a VI\2C let it run for a while\2C read every control and indicator\2C then ABORT it.\0A\0AWHY A SECOND RUNNER. lvai_run_and_read.vi wires Wait until done = TRUE\2C so it waits for termination. Every real application is an event or polling loop that never terminates on its own\3A the call times out and the VI keeps running. That is why a top-level VI could not be checked at all without first generating a scriptable copy of it - which is work the caller should not have to do to look at their own program.\0A\0AWHAT YOU GET IS A SNAPSHOT\2C and that is not a limitation to gloss over. The values are whatever the front panel held at the moment run for ms elapsed\3B a loop that has not reached its second state yet will show the first. Abort is not a stop button either - it kills the VI where it stands and runs NO cleanup the diagram may contain\2C so a VI that closes files or releases hardware on its normal path does not do that here.\0A\0AORDERING is enforced by the Case frame around the wait\2C not by layout\3A a structure produces its output tunnels only once every node inside it has finished\2C so Ctrl Val.Get All cannot read before the wait has elapsed. The frame also skips the wait when Run VI already failed\2C which turns a bad start into a fast answer instead of a pointless delay.\0A\0ADISABLED IS READ TOO\2C because a snapshot of values cannot show whether a control can be operated\2C and the VI leaves memory when this helper closes its reference - so nothing can look afterwards. It runs on its own error chain\3A a failed read leaves the two disabled indicators empty and never costs the snapshot or the abort.\0A\0ASIGNALS come after the first wait and before the snapshot. Each name in Signal Names is written with Value (Signaling)\2C which fires its Value Change event exactly as a click or a keystroke would\2C and signal gap ms is waited after each. The VI reference is threaded through that loop\2C so the snapshot cannot start before the last signal has been handled. Added 2026-09-26: the seventh ATM build passed every check including a start-up snapshot while its consumer read User Input before the user typed - a start-up snapshot cannot see a fault that needs an event to happen.">

